<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="-3" to="3" step="1" exclude="-1 0 1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="1" to="3" step="1" exclude="-1 0 1 $k $-k"/> 
  <function name="f">$k/x</function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPP">$fP</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPPP">$fPP</derivative>
  <derivative name="fP4">$fPPP</derivative>

  <function name="genTerm" variables="x n">$k*(-1)^n/$a^n*(x-$a)^n</function>
</setup>
<p>
  By responding to the following prompts, find the first several terms of the Taylor series of <me>f(x) = $f</me> centered at <m>a = $a</m> and express the Taylor series in sigma notation.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Complete the following table to assemble key information needed for the Taylor series of <m>f</m> centered at <m>a = $a</m>.
        <tabular>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f(x)=$f</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f($a)=</m><answer>$$f($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'(x)=</m><answer>$fP</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'($a)=</m><answer>$$fP($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f''(x)=</m><answer>$fPP</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f''($a)=</m><answer>$$fPP($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'''(x)=</m><answer>$fPPP</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'''($a)=</m><answer>$$fPPP($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f^{(4)}(x)=</m><answer>$fP4</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f^{(4)}($a)=</m><answer>$$fP4($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
              </tabular>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        State the first 5 terms of the Taylor series of <m>f</m> centered at <m>a = $a</m> by completing the blanks below; note that there is one blank per term and that several of the terms involve the variable <m>x</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>T_f(x) = </m><answer>$$f($a)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fP($a)(x-$a)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fPP($a)/2! * (x-$a)^2</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fPPP($a)/3! * (x-$a)^3</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fP4($a)/4! * (x-$a)^4</answer><m>+ \cdots</m>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        State the Taylor series of <m>f</m> centered at <m>a = $a</m> in sigma notation; it will be helpful to review your work in computing the values of <m>f'''($a)/3!</m> and <m>f^{(4)}($a)/4!</m> and to look for patterns that arise in these coefficients.
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>\displaystyle T_f(x) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} </m><answer>$genTerm</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>